  * `loadManifest` needs a browser, and the indexing is the part with a rule in
  * it.
  *
+ * **It is also where `card.image` becomes the object the views expect.** The
+ * manifest stores `{ w, h }` and `src/lib/image-shape.js` derives the five
+ * paths and the three `srcset` widths from the slug (see the comment on the
+ * image record in `scripts/build-manifest.mjs` for the gzip budget that is
+ * about). This is the one chokepoint every view goes through, so all ~30 call
+ * sites read the same fields they always did.
+ *
